

!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
!!                                                                                               !!
!!  A comprehensive study on low-temperature oxidation chemistry of cyclohexane. II.             !!
!!  Experimental and kinetic modeling investigation                                              !!
!!     Jiabiao Zou1, Hanfeng Jin2, Dapeng Liu2, Xiaoyuan Zhang1,2, Huaijiang Su3,                !!
!!     Jiuzhong Yang3, Aamir Farooq2, Yuyang Li1*                                                !!
!!  1. Key Laboratory for Power Machinery and Engineering of MOE, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, !!
!!     Shanghai 200240, P. R. China                                                              !!
!!  2. Clean Combustion Research Center, King Abdullah University of Science and Technology,     !!
!!     Thuwal 23955, Kingdom of Saudi Arabia                                                     !!
!!  3. National Synchrotron Radiation Laboratory, University of Science and Technology of China, !!
!!     Hefei, Anhui 230029, P. R. China                                                          !!
!!                                                                                               !!
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

!Be aware that the file requires CHEMKIN 4.1 or higher version to run.
!!!! Reaction classes
!!!  High Temperature Reaction Classes
!!!  1. Unimolecular decomposition of fuel
!!!  2. H-abstraction of fuel
!!!  3. Decomposition of cycloalkyl radical
!!!  4. Isomerization of cycloalkyl radical
!!!  5. H-abstraction of cycloalkene
!!!  6. Decomposition of cycloalkene
!!!  7. Retroene decomposition reaction
!!!  8. Reactions of cycloalkenyl radical with R'OO (HO2, CH3OO, C2H5O2 ...)
!!!  9. Decomposition of cycloalkenyl radical
!!!  10. Addition of OH to cycloalkene
!!!  
!!!  Low Temperature Reaction Classes
!!!  First O2 addition
!!!  11. R+O2=ROO
!!!  12. R+O2=cycloalkene+HO2
!!!  13. ROO+H2O2=ROOH+HO2
!!!  14. RH+ROO=R+ROOH
!!!  15. ROO+HO2=ROOH+O2
!!!  16. R+ROO=2RO or R+R'OO=RO+R'O
!!!  17. ROO+R'OO=RO+R'O+O2
!!!  18. ROO+ROO=ROH+R-H=O+O2
!!!  19. ROO=QOOH
!!!  20. ROO=cycloalkene+HO2
!!!  21. QOOH=cyclic ether/alkenal+OH
!!!  22. QOOH=cycloalkene+HO2
!!!  23. ROOH=RO+OH
!!!  24. RO decomposition
!!!  25. Decomposition of cyclic ether/ketone/aldehyde
!!!  Second O2 addition
!!!  26. QOOH+O2=OOQOOH
!!!  27. OOQOOH+RH/HO2=Q(OOH)2+R/O2
!!!  28. OOQOOH=keto-hydroperoxide+OH.
!!!  29. OOQOOH=P(OOH)2
!!!  30. OOQOOH=olefinic hydroperoxide+HO2
!!!  31. P(OOH)2=olefinic hydroperoxide+HO2
!!!  32. P(OOH)2=cyclic ether hydroperoxide+OH
!!!  33. P(OOH)2=alkenylhydroperoxide+OH
!!!  34. B-scission of P(OOH)2
!!!  35. KHP/OFHP/CEHP/AnHP/Q(OOH)2 decomposition
!!!  36. Decomposition of products from reaction classes 30-35
!!!  Third O2 addition
!!!  37. P(OOH)2+O2=OOP(OOH)2
!!!  38. OOP(OOH)2=keto-dihydroperoxide+OH
!!!  39. OOP(OOH)2=olefinic dihydroperoxide+HO2
!!!  40. OOP(OOH)2=T(OOH)3
!!!  41. T(OOH)3=olefinic dihydroperoxide+HO2
!!!  42. T(OOH)3=cyclic ether dihydroperoxide+OH
!!!  43. Decomposition of highly oxygenated molecule

ELEMENTS
C
H
N
O
AR
HE
END
!++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
